  #line-at(90.024pt, 380.81pt, "Abstract: Antichiral surface states, characterized by unidirectional propagation on ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 398.81pt, "parallel surfaces, offer unique potential for controlling classical waves. However, their ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 416.69pt, "realization typically relies on complex implementations of the two-dimensional ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 434.69pt, "modified Haldane model, limiting practical applications. Here, we propose a simplified ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 452.59pt, "scheme to realize such states within the nodal-line semimetal phase of a single-layer ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 470.59pt, "honeycomb lattice, by emulating the essential physics of the modified Haldane model ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 488.47pt, "through an introduced layer degree of freedom. Furthermore, we demonstrate that ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 506.47pt, "unequal vertical interlayer couplings can generate valley higher-order topological ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 524.35pt, "partial bandgaps, hosting coexisting one-dimensional hinge states and gapped antichiral ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 542.35pt, "surface states. We numerically verify these multiple topological states in acoustic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 560.23pt, "crystals, establishing a versatile platform for advanced wave manipulation. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(235.49pt, 603.55pt, "I. INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(111.02pt, 627.34pt, "Topological phases of matter [1,2] have attracted considerable attention owing to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 645.34pt, "their rich topological phenomena and potential device applications. This interest was ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 663.22pt, "ignited by the discovery of the quantum Hall effect [3,4] under strong magnetic fields, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 681.22pt, "which features chiral edge states that propagate unidirectionally along opposite sample ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 699.1pt, "edges. Building on this, the Haldane model [5]")
  #line-at(317.11pt, 699.1pt, "emerged as a pivotal theoretical model. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 717.1pt, "This model, defined on a honeycomb lattice, introduces periodic local magnetic fluxes ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 734.98pt, "that cancel out on average, eliminating the need for a net external magnetic field while ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 752.976pt, "still generating chiral edge states. It not only establishes a framework for the Chern ")
]

