#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 85.2pt, "insulator but also lays the groundwork for exploring exotic topological phases in time-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 103.1pt, "reversal-symmetry-invariant ")
  #line-at(240.17pt, 103.1pt, "systems. ")
  #line-at(294.79pt, 103.1pt, "Reversing ")
  #line-at(357.034pt, 103.1pt, "the ")
  #line-at(385.222pt, 103.1pt, "local ")
  #line-at(422.05pt, 103.1pt, "fluxes ")
  #line-at(464.986pt, 103.1pt, "on ")
  #line-at(490.534pt, 103.1pt, "the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 121.1pt, "sublattices modifies the Haldane model in a crucial way, yielding a distinct type of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 138.98pt, "boundary propagation: the antichiral edge states [6]. Unlike chiral edge states, antichiral ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 156.98pt, "modes propagate in the same direction along both parallel edges, compensated by a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 174.86pt, "counterflow in the bulk. This distinct bulk-boundary correspondence has sparked ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 192.86pt, "widespread interest [7-12] and inspired related concepts such as antihelical edge states ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 210.74pt, "[13]. However, the experimental realization of such antichiral edge states in electronic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 228.74pt, "systems remains challenging, as it requires precisely engineered artificial gauge fields. ")
  #line-at(111.02pt, 246.62pt, "Classical wave metamaterials, such as photonic and phononic crystals, provide a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 264.62pt, "versatile platform for realizing topological phenomena, benefiting from their ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 282.53pt, "macroscopic fabrication and tunability. To date, antichiral edge states have been ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 300.53pt, "realized using external magnetic fields in photonic systems [14-19], staggered air flows ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 318.41pt, "in acoustic systems [20,21], and intercomponent couplings in circuit lattices [22]. The ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 336.41pt, "unidirectional co-propagation of these states facilitates wave-manipulation effects such ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 354.29pt, "as wave splitting [21], paving the way for advanced acoustic wave control. More ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 372.29pt, "recently, three-dimensional (3D) layer-stacked systems have emerged as a powerful ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 390.17pt, "platform for engineering synthetic gauge fluxes. Implementations, such as time-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 408.17pt, "reversal-breaking magnetic Weyl photonic crystals [23], time-reversal-invariant ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 426.05pt, "photonic semimetals [24], and acoustic square lattice systems [25], have successfully ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 444.05pt, "demonstrated two-dimensional (2D) antichiral surface states that feature co-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 461.95pt, "propagating modes on opposing surfaces. However, a modified Haldane model that ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 479.95pt, "requires no external conditions has not been realized in acoustic systems. ")
  #line-at(111.02pt, 497.83pt, "Parallel to these developments, higher-order topology has risen to prominence, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 515.83pt, "attracting widespread interest [26-36]. In such phases, the co-dimension of the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 533.71pt, "topologically protected boundary states is equal to the difference between the system’s ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 551.71pt, "bulk dimensionality and its order. Their physical origin can be understood through ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 569.59pt, "frameworks like Wannier center configurations [28,29,31,33] and the mass-domain ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 587.59pt, "picture of boundary geometries [27,30,36]. The higher-order topology is extended to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 605.47pt, "topological semimetals, leading to higher-order topological semimetals [37]. These ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 623.47pt, "phases combine gapless bulk states characteristic of semimetals with lower-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 641.38pt, "dimensional boundary modes protected by higher-order topology. They have been ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 659.38pt, "realized in classical wave systems and can be categorized as higher-order Weyl ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 677.26pt, "semimetals [37-50], higher-order Dirac semimetals [51-56], and higher-order nodal-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 695.26pt, "line semimetals [57-63]. Notably, higher-order Weyl semimetals typically host one-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 713.14pt, "dimensional (1D) hinge states alongside 2D chiral surface states. Although antichiral ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 731.14pt, "hinge states have been theoretically predicted [8] in composite Haldane systems, the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 749.016pt, "relationship between the aforementioned 2D antichiral surface states and higher-order ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 767.016pt, "topology remains unexplored. Elucidating this connection could provide valuable ")
]

