  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(245.81pt, 354.41pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(262.85pt, 354.89pt, ". Simulated acoustic pressure distributions of the (b) ")
  #line-at(100.58pt, 372.77pt, "hinge, (c) surface, and (d) interface states. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(170.93pt, 414.05pt, "IV. CONCLUSIONS AND DISCUSSIONS ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(111.02pt, 437.81pt, "In summary, we have realized a modified Haldane model in a single-layer ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 455.71pt, "honeycomb acoustic lattice through engineered interlayer couplings. The resulting ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 473.71pt, "system provides a simplified platform for exploring exotic topological states. Our key ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 491.59pt, "findings are threefold.")
  #line-at(196.97pt, 491.59pt, "First, with only antichiral interlayer coupling, the system exhibits ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 509.59pt, "symmetry-protected nodal lines and hosts 2D antichiral surface states within each ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 527.59pt, "constant-")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(135.02pt, 527.59pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.62pt, 529.99pt, "𝑧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.74pt, 527.59pt, " subsystem. Second, introducing unequal vertical couplings splits these ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 545.47pt, "nodal lines into Weyl points, which serve as phase boundaries separating partial ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 563.35pt, "bandgaps that exhibit valley-dependent higher-order topology. Third, within these ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 581.35pt, "bandgaps, we find robust 1D hinge states, whereas the antichiral surface states existing ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 599.35pt, "in other ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.22pt, 599.35pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(139.82pt, 601.75pt, "𝑧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(144.98pt, 599.35pt, " slices become gapped. All theoretical predictions, based on a sequence of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 617.23pt, "two tight-binding models, are numerically verified in our designed acoustic crystals. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 635.14pt, "This work not only establishes a direct link between antichiral surface transport and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 653.14pt, "higher-order topology but also demonstrates concurrent multidimensional wave control ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 671.02pt, "by leveraging both 2D surface and 1D hinge states. Our platform thus opens avenues ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 689.02pt, "for designing advanced acoustic devices, such as wave splitters, topological sensors, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 706.9pt, "and robust waveguides. ")
]

